{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TA9DjzRnUWogPTdfp7iavZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information related to CoRL 2026, though the specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for CoRL 2026 are not comprehensively documented in the available search results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**For Historical Context:**\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, which may provide insights into the review criteria and process. For example, from CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor the complete and most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and the specific review form, you may want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) or the OpenReview portal for CoRL 2026, as the detailed reviewer guidelines may not yet be publicly available or may be communicated directly to invited reviewers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"bd43d3c7-f982-4e1b-9032-a0662a494ce5","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:25:59.724Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012u7X6nrZomz9Ng4A5gCkNm","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some information related to CoRL 2026, though the specific reviewer guidelines and review form details for CoRL 2026 are not comprehensively documented in the available search results.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal. Additionally, every author with 3 or more submissions must agree to serve as a reviewer.\n\n**Review Process:**\nThe aim is to have at least two reviewers per paper.\n\n**For Historical Context:**\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, which may provide insights into the review criteria and process. For example, from CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nFor the complete and most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and the specific review form, you may want to check the official CoRL 2026 website (corl.org) or the OpenReview portal for CoRL 2026, as the detailed reviewer guidelines may not yet be publicly available or may be communicated directly to invited reviewers."],"durationSeconds":5.6113054049999995}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GWExzbZhRX6bRnq77wU7Sh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737\"}]\n\nI found some information about CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specifically for CoRL 2025. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nFor regular papers at CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers are instructed to treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. All CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nHowever, I was unable to find specific information about CoRL 2025's complete reviewer guidelines, review form, or detailed scoring criteria in these search results. For the most current and detailed CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2025 website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"de95d573-93f3-4ceb-9609-daa8f89b82cb","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:26:00.316Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GASBp7eg3ULHGAJKJ67dxz","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Can LLM feedback enhance review quality? A randomized study of 20K   reviews at ICLR 2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.09737"}]},"I found some information about CoRL 2024 reviewer guidelines, but not specifically for CoRL 2025. Based on the search results, here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nFor regular papers at CoRL 2024, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers are instructed to treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\n## Desk Rejection Criteria\n\nPapers can be desk rejected for one of three reasons: formatting issues, anonymity violation, or scope. All CoRL submissions must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning through either explicitly addressing a learning question for physical robots or testing the proposed learning solution on physical robots.\n\nHowever, I was unable to find specific information about CoRL 2025's complete reviewer guidelines, review form, or detailed scoring criteria in these search results. For the most current and detailed CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2025 website directly."],"durationSeconds":5.706578614}}
