{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017xccqP3ouyhWF374wq7csK","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines - Limited Information Available\n\nBased on the provided web content, **the document does not contain complete reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, numerical rating scales, or review form structure**.\n\n## What IS Included:\n\n**Review Criteria:**\nThe page specifies that submissions are evaluated on:\n- \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- \"relevance to robotic learning\"\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications:**\nReviewers should demonstrate expertise with \"a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\"\n\n## What IS NOT Included:\n\n- Numerical scoring scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10)\n- Specific rating definitions\n- Review form structure/template\n- Evaluation dimensions beyond general criteria\n- Decision categories or recommendation options\n\n**Note:** The full reviewer guidelines appear to be on another page or document not provided in this excerpt. You may need to access the complete CoRL 2024 review submission portal or contact the organizing committee for the complete review form."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"229a0a3e-fce7-431b-af91-9e5b5e611c59","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:26:12.926Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134214,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines - Limited Information Available\n\nBased on the provided web content, **the document does not contain complete reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, numerical rating scales, or review form structure**.\n\n## What IS Included:\n\n**Review Criteria:**\nThe page specifies that submissions are evaluated on:\n- \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- \"degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact\"\n- \"relevance to robotic learning\"\n\n**Reviewer Qualifications:**\nReviewers should demonstrate expertise with \"a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\"\n\n## What IS NOT Included:\n\n- Numerical scoring scales (e.g., 1-5, 1-10)\n- Specific rating definitions\n- Review form structure/template\n- Evaluation dimensions beyond general criteria\n- Decision categories or recommendation options\n\n**Note:** The full reviewer guidelines appear to be on another page or document not provided in this excerpt. You may need to access the complete CoRL 2024 review submission portal or contact the organizing committee for the complete review form.","durationMs":3987,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019kqHNPyKd2zYZML3p7EqT7","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Key Review Dimensions\n\nThe CoRL 2023 review process evaluates submissions across six main criteria:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new? Is the work a novel combination of well-known techniques?\"\n\n2. **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound? Are claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results)?\"\n\n3. **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written? Is it well organized?\"\n\n4. **Significance**: \"Are the results important? Are others (researchers or practitioners) likely to use the ideas or build on them?\"\n\n5. **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method?\"\n\n6. **Limitations**: Papers must include a limitations section; honestly reported limitations should be treated favorably.\n\n## Review Structure\n\nReviews require two main components:\n- **Paper Summary**: Restate contributions in your own words rather than copying abstracts\n- **Main Review**: Detailed evaluation across the six dimensions above\n\n## Important Notes\n\n**No numerical scoring scales or rating scales are specified** in the provided guidelines. The document emphasizes constructive feedback and mentions avoiding common reviewer mistakes, but does not detail specific point systems or ranking categories for scoring papers.\n\nThe review process spans three months with phases for bidding (June 9-11), reviews (deadline July 19), discussion (August 3-15), and final decisions (August 16-25)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"7ef15762-d142-4fa7-9966-7d912e69532d","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:26:15.043Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Key Review Dimensions\n\nThe CoRL 2023 review process evaluates submissions across six main criteria:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new? Is the work a novel combination of well-known techniques?\"\n\n2. **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound? Are claims well supported (e.g., by theoretical analysis or experimental results)?\"\n\n3. **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written? Is it well organized?\"\n\n4. **Significance**: \"Are the results important? Are others (researchers or practitioners) likely to use the ideas or build on them?\"\n\n5. **Relevance**: \"Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method?\"\n\n6. **Limitations**: Papers must include a limitations section; honestly reported limitations should be treated favorably.\n\n## Review Structure\n\nReviews require two main components:\n- **Paper Summary**: Restate contributions in your own words rather than copying abstracts\n- **Main Review**: Detailed evaluation across the six dimensions above\n\n## Important Notes\n\n**No numerical scoring scales or rating scales are specified** in the provided guidelines. The document emphasizes constructive feedback and mentions avoiding common reviewer mistakes, but does not detail specific point systems or ranking categories for scoring papers.\n\nThe review process spans three months with phases for bidding (June 9-11), reviews (deadline July 19), discussion (August 3-15), and final decisions (August 16-25).","durationMs":5632,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
