{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XPq7dbBjqGEX2KyD8x5L59","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Review Information\n\nBased on the webpage content provided, here's what I can extract:\n\n**Rating Scale:** The data indicates ratings ranging from 1.70 to 4.00, with an average of 3.01 (standard deviation: 0.37).\n\n**Acceptance Rate:** CoRL 2024 had a 39.34% acceptance rate, with 264 papers accepted out of 671 total submissions.\n\n**Review Categories:** All 264 accepted papers were designated as posters, with no oral presentations or spotlight papers listed for the acceptance tier.\n\n**Withdrawal Data:** Only 1 submission (0.15%) involved a post-decision withdrawal.\n\n**Limitations:** The webpage does not explicitly detail the specific scoring criteria, overall recommendation frameworks, or comprehensive review guidelines. The interface mentions metric options for viewing \"Rating,\" \"Confidence,\" and \"Replies\" data from OpenReview, but the actual scoring rubric and evaluation standards are not documented in this content.\n\nThe statistics come from OpenReview submissions data for the conference held in Munich, Germany in 2024."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"5792d17c-3018-464b-b2cf-41feed9de9c9","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:26:54.384Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":222526,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Review Information\n\nBased on the webpage content provided, here's what I can extract:\n\n**Rating Scale:** The data indicates ratings ranging from 1.70 to 4.00, with an average of 3.01 (standard deviation: 0.37).\n\n**Acceptance Rate:** CoRL 2024 had a 39.34% acceptance rate, with 264 papers accepted out of 671 total submissions.\n\n**Review Categories:** All 264 accepted papers were designated as posters, with no oral presentations or spotlight papers listed for the acceptance tier.\n\n**Withdrawal Data:** Only 1 submission (0.15%) involved a post-decision withdrawal.\n\n**Limitations:** The webpage does not explicitly detail the specific scoring criteria, overall recommendation frameworks, or comprehensive review guidelines. The interface mentions metric options for viewing \"Rating,\" \"Confidence,\" and \"Replies\" data from OpenReview, but the actual scoring rubric and evaluation standards are not documented in this content.\n\nThe statistics come from OpenReview submissions data for the conference held in Munich, Germany in 2024.","durationMs":4363,"url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/"}}
