{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VpdcaRPa42TW2SZ5gT2L3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've spent enough time trying to find the exact CoRL review form. Based on what I've gathered:\n\n1. CoRL 2024 had a ~39% acceptance rate\n2. CoRL reviews average around 3.01 on what appears to be a 1-5 scale\n3. Review dimensions include: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n4. Papers are evaluated on \"significance and novelty of the results\" and \"relevance to robotic learning\"\n\nLet me use a standard robotics/ML conference review scale similar to what CoRL uses. Based on Paper Copilot's statistics showing average ratings around 3.01 with a max of 4.0, it appears CoRL uses a 1-5 scale (or possibly 1-4). Actually, looking more carefully at the statistics showing ratings between 1.70 and 4.00, this looks like it could be derived from a scale of 1-5 or a larger scale. \n\nI'll proceed with a reasonable CoRL-style review using the standard ML conference format with a 1-5 rating scale, since that aligns with the observed average of 3.01 and the distribution I'm seeing in the data.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":63524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"29434d3a-ff1e-4166-af12-0eb4cb15f5a0"}
