{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018r8z8ELTxzmzKM5TF9zjBi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've spent a lot of effort trying to find the exact CoRL review form. Let me proceed with what I know. Based on my research:\n\n1. CoRL 2024 acceptance rate: ~39%\n2. CoRL reviews use a scale where the average is around 3.0 (from Paper Copilot statistics showing range 1.70-4.00 with mean 3.01)\n3. Review dimensions: Originality, Quality/Soundness, Clarity, Significance, Relevance to robot learning, Limitations\n4. CoRL uses OpenReview\n\n\n5. The scale appears to be 1-5 based on those statistics, which aligns with the 3.01 mean and 39% acceptance rate\n\n—papers averaging around 3.5-4.0 would be accepted while the overall average including rejections lands at 3.0. Now I'll set up the review structure with two parallel reviewers handling different aspects, then bring them together for a roundtable discussion before finalizing the report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":65348,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":291},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"f7233646-b796-4a8d-8360-5c028a491a01"}
