{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011m7osVDCtkF5E8wZjU12Bf","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/occsafe_vla/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: AAAI 2027\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: aaai25\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"Director confirmed: use AAAI-25 template (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\usepackage{aaai25}), format compatible with AAAI 2027\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 7\\\\n  abstract_deadline: 2026-07-21\\\\n  deadline: 2026-07-28\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    BEV occupancy auxiliary supervision during VLA fine-tuning induces implicit collision\\\\n    avoidance as an emergent property of 3D spatial understanding, without explicit safety training.\\\\n  framing: \\\\\\\"Option C (OccSafe-VLA system paper) primary, Option B (analysis) fallback\\\\\\\"\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-20T20:00:00Z\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: VLAs achieve high TSR (~88%) but collide frequently (CAR ~64%)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: 15+ spatial-VLA methods never evaluate collision safety; all safety-VLA methods ignore spatial representation advances\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: BEV occ auxiliary supervision forces vision encoder to learn 3D boundary awareness; OCC-CBF provides explicit safety conditioned on learned occ features\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Results: [TODO — pending MVP experiments]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1000\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: TSR=88% but CAR=64% — 36% collision rate; Task 5 TSR=80% CAR=0% exemplifies task success ≠ behavioral safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Diagnosis: 2D pretrained vision encoders learn semantic-action mapping but lack 3D object boundary understanding\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: Spatial-VLA (15+ methods) and safety-VLA (4+ methods) developed in complete isolation — no one tested the interaction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Insight: BEV occupancy encodes workspace boundaries; occ aux supervision during fine-tuning injects spatial awareness into vision encoder\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mechanism: Safety as emergent property of 3D understanding — zero inference cost, no explicit safety training\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: [C1] First spatial-safety interaction study for VLAs; [C2] OccSafe-VLA (occ aux + OCC-CBF); [C3] Actionable safe VLA design principles\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    figures: [fig1_overview]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT for base architecture\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"VLSA/AEGIS for benchmark and CAR baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Representative spatial-VLA methods for gap claim\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    pre_writable: true\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.1 3D Representations for VLA (~500w): 15+ methods — DepthVLA, SpatialVLA, Spatial Forcing, GST-VLA, StemVLA, 3D-CAVLA, CorridorVLA, ST-VLA, AugVLA-3D, Evo-0, GeoAware-VLA, GeoVLA, PointVLA, SG-VLA, SA-VLA — improve spatial reasoning via depth/point cloud/implicit alignment/Gaussian but NONE evaluate collision safety metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.2 Safe Robot Manipulation with VLAs (~350w): AEGIS/VLSA (plug-in CBF, +59.16% CAR), SafeVLA (RL-based, NeurIPS 2025 Spotlight), CoFreeVLA (semi-internalized risk), Safe-Night VLA (thermal+CBF) — none leverage 3D spatial representation advances\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§2.3 Occupancy in Robotics (~250w): OccVLA (occ+VLA for AD, zero inference cost), OGM-CBF (discrete grid→CBF for navigation), Learning to Nudge (learned composable DCBF for manipulation) — convergent evidence that occupancy-informed barriers outperform Euclidean-distance barriers, but untransferred to VLA representation space\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap statement (~100w): No work evaluates the interaction between spatial representation choice and collision safety outcome\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    pre_writable: true\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.1 Problem Formulation (~200w): VLA π(a|o,l); define TSR and CAR formally; goal = improve CAR without TSR degradation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.2 BEV Occupancy Auxiliary Head (~400w): lightweight MLP from DINOv2 patch features → 64×64 BEV grid; FocalLoss; zero inference cost (head discarded at test time)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.3 Training Pipeline (~300w): OpenVLA-OFT base + L_total = L_action + λ·L_occ; gradient flow to vision encoder (occ_detach=False); occ_weight=0.1\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§3.4 OCC-CBF (~300w): h_occ(x) = f_θ(z_occ, x_robot); spectral normalization for Lipschitz continuity; adaptive activation; [PLACEHOLDER for detailed formulation pending OCC-CBF implementation]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      pi: \\\\\\\"VLA policy π(a|o,l)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      o_t: \\\\\\\"visual observation at time t\\\\\\\"\\\\n      l: \\\\\\\"language instruction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      a_t: \\\\\\\"7-DOF action (delta end-effector pose)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      L_occ: \\\\\\\"BEV occupancy prediction loss (FocalLoss)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      lambda: \\\\\\\"occ_weight hyperparameter\\\\\\\"\\\\n      z_occ: \\\\\\\"learned occupancy features from vision encoder\\\\\\\"\\\\n      h_occ: \\\\\\\"occupancy-conditioned barrier function\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 1600\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.1 Benchmark (~100w): SafeLIBERO Level I/II, LIBERO-Spatial suite (10 tasks)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.2 Evaluation Protocol (~100w): TSR, CAR (L1 displacement, threshold=0.001, aligned with VLSA); 20 rollouts/task × 3 seeds; paired t-test + Cohen's d + 95% CI\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.3 Experimental Conditions (~100w): vanilla, +occ, +occ_detach, +depth, +random_occ; with/without AEGIS CBF\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.4 Implementation Details (~100w): OpenVLA-OFT 7B, 50K steps, LoRA rank 32, batch 8, lr 5e-4, seeds 42/43/44\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.5 Main Results: [TODO]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.6 Ablation Study: [TODO]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§4.7 Analysis: [TODO — per-task breakdown, gradient flow, attention patterns]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [mvp_vanilla_s0, mvp_vanilla_s1, mvp_vanilla_s2, mvp_occ_s0, mvp_occ_s1, mvp_occ_s2]\\\\n    tables: [tab1_main, tab2_ablation]\\\\n    figures: [fig2_pertask]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 400\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: First work connecting spatial representations and collision safety in VLAs\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: single architecture (OpenVLA-OFT 7B), single benchmark (LIBERO/SafeLIBERO), sim-only, n=3 seeds\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: multiple architectures, real-robot, predicted occ from monocular RGB, dense clutter extension\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_overview\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: paperbanana\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"OccSafe-VLA system overview: OpenVLA-OFT backbone + BEV occ auxiliary head from DINOv2 patches, gradient flow, OCC-CBF at inference\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"A lightweight BEV occ head during training forces the vision encoder to learn 3D spatial structure; at inference the head is discarded (zero cost) but spatial awareness persists, enabling implicit collision avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Left panel: training phase (occ head attached, gradient arrows from L_occ through encoder)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Right panel: inference phase (occ head removed, safety emerges from spatially-aware encoder)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Color: blue=frozen, orange=trainable, green=auxiliary (discarded at inference)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: introduction\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:6\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deferred: true\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_pertask\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Per-task TSR vs CAR for vanilla baseline showing layout-determined collision\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Vanilla CAR is layout-determined (bimodal: tasks with nearby obstacles have CAR≈0%, isolated objects have CAR≈100%), proving the model has zero active collision avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Grouped bar: TSR (blue) and CAR (red) per task\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Annotate T5: 80% success but 0% collision avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Pattern B: annotation arrows highlighting the paradox\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: mvp_vanilla_s0, mvp_vanilla_s1, mvp_vanilla_s2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deferred: true\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_qualitative\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Trajectory comparison vanilla vs +occ on high-collision tasks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Occ supervision causes the robot to approach from collision-free angles rather than direct paths that clip obstacles\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Side-by-side top-down trajectory view\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Red X for collision points, shaded obstacle boundaries\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: mvp_vanilla_s0, mvp_occ_s0\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"2:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deferred: true\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_main\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Main results on SafeLIBERO Level I. TSR: task success rate (↑). CAR: collision avoidance rate (↑). Best bold, second-best underlined. Mean ± std over 3 seeds.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Condition, Spatial_Rep, Safety_Mech, TSR, CAR]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: mvp_vanilla_s0, mvp_vanilla_s1, mvp_vanilla_s2, mvp_occ_s0, mvp_occ_s1, mvp_occ_s2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Paired t-test p-values in footnote; Cohen's d for effect size\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deferred: true\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab2_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Ablation study isolating occupancy specificity, gradient flow necessity, and auxiliary loss control.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Condition, Description, TSR, CAR, Delta_CAR]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: [TODO — post-MVP D005 experiments]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"+occ (full)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deferred: true\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 45\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"3D spatial representations for vision-language-action models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"safety and collision avoidance for robot manipulation VLAs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"occupancy-based planning and barrier functions in robotics\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"spatial-vla\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"3D spatial representation vision language action model 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"depth VLA manipulation spatial reasoning auxiliary\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"implicit 3D supervision VLA robot manipulation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"point cloud VLA spatial awareness\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SpatialVLA (arXiv 2501.15830, RSS 2026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Spatial Forcing (arXiv 2510.12276, ICLR 2026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DepthVLA (arXiv 2510.13375)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"GST-VLA (arXiv 2603.09079)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"StemVLA (arXiv 2602.23721)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"3D-CAVLA (arXiv 2505.05800)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"CorridorVLA (arXiv 2604.21241)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 15\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"safety-vla\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"safe VLA collision avoidance manipulation 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"safety constraint vision language action model barrier\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AEGIS/VLSA (arXiv 2512.11891)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SafeVLA (arXiv 2503.03480, NeurIPS 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"CoFreeVLA (arXiv 2601.21712)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"occupancy-robotics\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"occupancy map barrier function robot collision avoidance\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"occupancy VLA autonomous driving supervision\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"learned barrier function manipulation dense clutter\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OccVLA (arXiv 2509.05578)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OGM-CBF (arXiv 2405.10703)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Learning to Nudge (arXiv 2601.02686)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"infrastructure\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA fine-tuning VLA recipe 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"VLA evaluation benchmark safety\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA-OFT (arXiv 2502.19645)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA (arXiv 2406.09246)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  # Pre-writable sections (current phase):\\\\n  - experiments_setup    # §4.1-4.4 only — DONE\\\\n  - method              # §3.1-3.4\\\\n  - related_work        # §2.1-2.3 + gap\\\\n  # Deferred until experiments complete:\\\\n  # - experiments_results (§4.5-4.7)\\\\n  # - introduction\\\\n  # - abstract\\\\n  # - conclusion\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 11278, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tiuv7BknzVCPhTpc13ZXwG","session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"13bbce4d-0d04-4796-829a-97b9036230a5","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:29:34.263Z"}
