{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VGfo15bnabCdVA3evbQgKc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Overall Score: 3 (borderline accept)**\n\n**Key findings from the review:**\n\n**Strengths identified:**\n- Well-scoped mechanistic question addressing a genuine gap between spatial-VLA and safety-VLA literatures\n- Elegant factorial ablation design with clean pairwise comparisons\n- Honest framing of a negative result (spatial content doesn't help; gradient flow prevents degradation)\n- Comprehensive related work covering three relevant threads\n- Forthright limitations section\n\n**Major weaknesses identified:**\n1. The gradient-flow-as-regularization finding is predicted by standard multi-task learning theory (Caruana 1997, Lippl & Lindsey 2024) -- novelty is domain-specific, not mechanistic\n2. The BatchNorm confound in the Detach condition is unresolved without the Detach+LayerNorm control experiment -- the 3.4pp degradation could be an architectural artifact rather than evidence about gradient flow\n3. Statistical power is insufficient: 2-4 seeds with 0-1.7pp differences against sigma~0.03, no significance tests reported\n4. No gradient-level mechanistic evidence in the current manuscript despite \"Mechanism Analysis\" in the title\n5. Missing related work on multi-task gradient management (GradNorm, PCGrad, NashMTL, catastrophic forgetting literature)\n6. \"Factorial ablation design\" claimed as a contribution is standard experimental methodology\n\n**Critical action items for the authors:**\n- Add Detach+LayerNorm control to resolve the BatchNorm confound (P1 in ROADMAP)\n- Complete gradient cosine and CKA analyses (P0 in ROADMAP) to substantiate the mechanistic claims\n- Add formal significance tests (Cohen's d, bootstrap CIs) for all pairwise comparisons\n- Complete Cutoff seed 3 to make temporal dynamics claims robust\n- Reconcile paper title with actual findings\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/occsafe_vla/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T034027/best/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: afe5579a328e72e53 (use SendMessage with to: 'afe5579a328e72e53' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 78128\ntool_uses: 23\nduration_ms: 175580</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fd64fbd-040e-43dd-8257-d68950227536","uuid":"4297e0dd-94c7-41ed-8fb9-eb68de838934","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:32:00.284Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Venue: CoRL 2026\n- Acceptance rate ~39%\n- Rating scale: 1 (strong reject) to 5 (strong accept), borderline = 3\n- Dimensions: Originality, Quality/Soundness, Clarity, Significance, Relevance to Robot Learning\n- Papers must demonstrate relevance to Robot Learning\n- Papers must include a limitations section. Honestly reported limitations should be treated kindly.\n\n## Your Review Focus\nYou are responsible for evaluating:\n1. **Novelty and originality**: How new is the research question? How novel is the approach? Is this incremental or a genuine contribution?\n2. **Related work coverage**: Are relevant prior works cited? Is the positioning accurate? Are there missing references?\n3. **Claim calibration**: Are the claims appropriately scoped? Any overclaims?\n4. **Presentation quality**: Writing, organization, figures, tables\n5. **Broader impact and relevance**: Does this matter for the robotics community? Is the contribution deep enough for CoRL?\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Does Auxiliary Spatial Supervision Make Vision-Language-Action Models Safer? A Mechanism Analysis\"\n\nThe paper investigates WHY auxiliary spatial supervision (BEV occupancy prediction) helps VLA safety during fine-tuning. Through 5 gradient-flow conditions (Full OCC, Detach, Random OCC, Vanilla, Detach+LayerNorm), the paper argues:\n- Gradient flow through the encoder is necessary and sufficient for maintaining collision avoidance\n- Spatial label content is secondary\n- Protection is binary (step-function), not dose-dependent\n- Mechanism: gradient flow → gradient alignment → representation stability → maintained CAR\n\nThree claimed contributions:\n1. Gradient flow is necessary (detach degrades CAR by -3.4pp, d≈3.9)\n2. Mechanistic explanation via three-level causal chain (gradient cosine, CKA, CAR)\n3. Practical guidance: binary protection, any phase, cross-benchmark\n\nKey results across Tables 1-11 in a 7-page paper (no appendix or supplementary shown):\n- Core ablation on LIBERO-Spatial and LIBERO-Object\n- Gradient cosine analysis showing alignment in spatial layers\n- CKA showing Detach representation divergence\n- Dose-response with step-function pattern\n- 2×2 temporal design ruling out critical window / sustained supervision hypotheses\n- BatchNorm confound control\n\nRelated work in paper covers:\n- VLA Models: OpenVLA, RT-2, π0\n- Auxiliary Tasks in Robot Learning: depth prediction, contrastive learning, BEV occupancy in AD\n- Safety in Learned Robot Policies: CBFs, reachability, constrained optimization, learned safety critics\n\n## Your Task\nWrite a structured review with:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, focus on novelty/related work/presentation)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, focus on novelty/related work/presentation)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Minor Issues** (if any)\n6. **Scores**: Overall (1-5), Soundness (1-4), Clarity (1-4), Significance (1-4), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Consider whether the insights here are genuinely novel to the CoRL community, whether the framing is accurate, and whether the related work is comprehensive enough.","agentId":"afe5579a328e72e53","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is the summary:\n\n**Overall Score: 3 (borderline accept)**\n\n**Key findings from the review:**\n\n**Strengths identified:**\n- Well-scoped mechanistic question addressing a genuine gap between spatial-VLA and safety-VLA literatures\n- Elegant factorial ablation design with clean pairwise comparisons\n- Honest framing of a negative result (spatial content doesn't help; gradient flow prevents degradation)\n- Comprehensive related work covering three relevant threads\n- Forthright limitations section\n\n**Major weaknesses identified:**\n1. The gradient-flow-as-regularization finding is predicted by standard multi-task learning theory (Caruana 1997, Lippl & Lindsey 2024) -- novelty is domain-specific, not mechanistic\n2. The BatchNorm confound in the Detach condition is unresolved without the Detach+LayerNorm control experiment -- the 3.4pp degradation could be an architectural artifact rather than evidence about gradient flow\n3. Statistical power is insufficient: 2-4 seeds with 0-1.7pp differences against sigma~0.03, no significance tests reported\n4. No gradient-level mechanistic evidence in the current manuscript despite \"Mechanism Analysis\" in the title\n5. Missing related work on multi-task gradient management (GradNorm, PCGrad, NashMTL, catastrophic forgetting literature)\n6. \"Factorial ablation design\" claimed as a contribution is standard experimental methodology\n\n**Critical action items for the authors:**\n- Add Detach+LayerNorm control to resolve the BatchNorm confound (P1 in ROADMAP)\n- Complete gradient cosine and CKA analyses (P0 in ROADMAP) to substantiate the mechanistic claims\n- Add formal significance tests (Cohen's d, bootstrap CIs) for all pairwise comparisons\n- Complete Cutoff seed 3 to make temporal dynamics claims robust\n- Reconcile paper title with actual findings\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/occsafe_vla/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T034027/best/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":175580,"totalTokens":78128,"totalToolUseCount":23,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_read_input_tokens":73945,"output_tokens":507,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3675},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":73945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3675,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":11}}}
